<title>TAIWAN: Formosa Plastics issues T$5.0 bln bonds.</title>
<headline>Formosa Plastics issues T$5.0 bln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Formosa Plastics Corp said on Wednesday it would issue corporate bonds worth T$5.0 billion.</p>
<p>The bonds would be used to collect long-term funds and repay short-term debts for the company, a Formosa statement said.</p>
<p>The term of the bonds would not exceed seven years and coupon rate on the bonds would not exceed 6.85 percent, the statement said.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (-5080815)</p>
</text>
